# Ubuntu and Debian

The current GitHub Actions workflow runs the standard build and tests on
`ubuntu-latest`; this is not evidence for every Ubuntu or Debian release. See
`INSTALL` for the portable source-build procedure.

For Ubuntu, the CI workflow uses development packages named
`libsctp-dev`, `libgnutls28-dev`, `libgcrypt-dev`, and `libidn2-dev`, in
addition to CMake, C and C++ compilers, Bison 3.0+, Flex, and pkg-config. If
SCTP is not available, configure with `-DDISABLE_SCTP=ON`. Optional extension
dependencies include `libpq-dev` for `app_acct`, MySQL development files for
`app_sip` and `app_diameap`, `libxml2-dev` for `dict_legacy_xml`, and
`python3-dev` plus `swig` for `dbg_interactive`.

Debian packaging metadata and rules are in `contrib/debian`. The checked-in
Debian changelog currently identifies the source package as 2.0.0, while the
CMake project version is 1.6.1. This metadata difference is not reconciled by
these instructions; no successful build of a 2.0.0 package is asserted.
Review the current packaging files and build environment before producing or
installing packages. Do not rely on old repository, debhelper, or package
installation commands from prior versions of this file.
